      "message": "I could do this and Daisuke had the same request. However, in this instance I don\u0027t think that the deltas from that CL are helpful for what /board/nucleo-g4 represents. The original CL was merely an EC project skeleton. This CL basically undoes that and adds a new board project for nucleo-g4. All this board project does is expose the EC console, flash the LED, and output the system clock to a gpio pin. /board/honeybuns as I used it initially was merged into board/quiche\n\nSince I know that it builds and can be loaded on the STM32 nucleo-g4 dev board, I thought it was worth keeping as I see other nucleo boards exist. Stated another way, this CL is if I had deleted board/honeybuns and then added board/nucleo-g431rb in a subsequent CL.",
